[direction] d-03 -> blocked (Tool budget (10 calls) exhausted after core grid/scan/X-ray/BEST checks and exclusion plot; SBL contour digitization/overlay and literature search for loophole mechanisms could not run. DNS failure on web_search also blocked non-standard mechanism survey.)
**Blocked — Thermalization threshold, exclusion plane overlay, and viability assessment with non-standard loopholes and eV vs keV contrast.** Tool budget (10 calls) exhausted after core grid/scan/X-ray/BEST checks and exclusion plot; SBL contour digitization/overlay and literature search for loophole mechanisms could not run. DNS failure on web_search also blocked non-standard mechanism survey. Direction d-03 established quantitative thermalization and exclusion results for eV sterile neutrinos in standard Dodelson-Widrow cosmology; SBL contour overlay and non-standard loophole literature remain open due to tool budget exhaustion. What was done (all local execution): - Thermalization threshold grid: 27 points (m_s=0.5,1,3 eV x sin^2 2theta=1e-4 to 1) shows sharp transition. For all three eV masses, sin^2 2theta=1e-3 gives Delta N_eff=0.40 (Delta chi2 BBN=0.62, allowed), sin^2 2theta=3e-3 gives Delta N_eff=1.0 (Delta chi2=23.1, excluded at 95% CL). Threshold for near-complete thermalization is sin^2 2theta ~1-3e-3. File: sterile_nu_grid_DW_b2a7f6.csv. - BBN/relic-density exclusion plane scan: 3600 points (m_s 0.1-10 eV, sin^2 2theta 1e-4 to 1, DW). 2597/3600 BBN-excluded (Delta chi2>3.84) and 2362/3600 overclose (Omega_s h2>0.12). Maximum BBN-allowed mixing is sin^2 2theta=0.00122 at all sampled eV masses. Files: scan_DW_9bdb63.csv and .npz. - Canonical BEST SBL best-fit (m_s=1.14 eV, Delta m2=1.3 eV2, sin^2 2theta=0.42) predicts Delta N_eff=1.0 (N_eff=4.044), Omega_s h2=29.3 (244x observed DM 0.12), BBN Yp=0.2596 (obs 0.2449+/-0.004) and D/H=2.78e-5 (obs 2.547+/-0.025e-5) with Delta chi2=23.1 vs SM, 6.2 sigma tension with Planck N_eff=2.99+/-0.17 (33 sigma for CMB-S4 sigma=0.03). - eV vs keV contrast: keV benchmark m_s=7.1 keV, sin^2 2theta=7e-11 gives E_gamma=m_s/2=3.55 keV, lifetime 5.8e27 s (1.8e20 yr), excluded by NuSTAR M31 and XMM-Newton blank sky. eV SBL mixing 0.1-0.5 is 9-10 orders of magnitude larger than keV DM mixing 2e-11 to 2e-10; eV decay photons at 0.00057 keV are unobservable vs keV X-ray line. - Exclusion plane figure produced: Figure 2 (exclusion_scan_DW_9bdb63.png) from 3600-point scan showing BBN-excluded and overclosure regions with Omega_DM line and X-ray/Lyman-alpha limits. What was not done: - SBL preferred contour overlay (LSND/MiniBooNE, BEST, reactor) digitized from literature onto exclusion plane - requires get_paper_figures and manual digitization, not executed before budget limit. - Non-standard suppression literature search (large lepton asymmetry L~1e-2, secret interactions, low reheating) - web_search failed with DNS error and budget exhausted. - Formatted thermalization scan plot and X-ray contrast table as publication-ready figures - numbers established but not plotted. All outputs in /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-sbl-neff/runs/261107_171616/
