**Blocked — Literature survey of SBL anomaly status 2024-2026: MicroBooNE, STEREO, PROSPECT, BEST/gallium, reactor flux re-evaluation, global 3+1 fits.** Tool budget reached after 6 web_search calls (2 DNS failures); no remaining calls for read_arxiv_chunk, cite, or get_paper_figures. At least 5 arXiv citations with verbatim quotes including arXiv:2504.16590 and 1-2 extracted figures required by success criteria could not be executed. Literature survey partially completed via web search and BBN server metadata; full citation and figure extraction blocked by tool budget exhaustion. Established: MicroBooNE 170-ton LArTPC on Booster beam saw no electron-neutrino excess 2021-2024, June 2024 combined analysis excluded MiniBooNE electron-neutrino interpretation at >99% CL and Dec 2025 data exclude single light sterile LSND/MiniBooNE at 95% CL; STEREO final 119 reactor-on-day dataset (Dec 2024) at 2.5-7 m baselines shows no L/E oscillation and excludes canonical reactor anomaly eV-sterile region at >99.9% CL, with PROSPECT (segmented detector ~7 m from HFIR HEU core) + STEREO combined excluding most reactor anomaly space and attributing 5-6% rate deficit and 5 MeV bump to flux-prediction biases in nuclear data; gallium anomaly (GALLEX/SAGE 51Cr calibration, BEST confirmation >5 sigma, Delta m2 ~1 eV2 sin2 2theta ~0.4) persists but in tension with reactor/accelerator nulls, with arXiv:2504.16590 (Ciuffoli et al., Apr 2025) proposing independent test using same 51Cr source via electron-neutrino scattering; cosmology N_eff = 2.99 +/- 0.17 (Planck 2018 TT,TE,EE+lowE+lensing+BAO, SM 3.044) excludes fully thermalized sterile Delta N_eff ~1 (N_eff ~4) at high significance, with BBN Yp = 0.2449 +/- 0.004 and D/H = 2.547 +/- 0.025e-5 providing complementary limits (BBN fit valid N_eff 2.044-6.044, omega_b h2 0.019-0.0257, exclusion Delta chi2 >3.84, valid m_s <~100 keV). Not done: no arXiv chunks read, no verbatim quotes cited, no .bib created, no figures extracted (0 of 2-4 required), no global 3+1 fit tension quantification, no Planck+ACT+DESI BAO 2024-2025 update beyond Planck 2018 value. Findings posted as f-009, f-010, f-011, f-015, f-016, f-017; dead end x-03 records citation/figure failure.
