[direction] d-06 -> blocked (Tool budget exhausted after 4 web_search + 2 predict_sterile_nu calls; no read_arxiv_chunk/cite calls available to extract verbatim quotes and arXiv IDs for loophole papers. Quantitative per-mechanism constraints remain open.)
**Blocked — Quantify non-standard loopholes required to reconcile eV sterile with N_eff=2.99+/-0.17 and their independent constraints.** Tool budget exhausted after 4 web_search + 2 predict_sterile_nu calls; no read_arxiv_chunk/cite calls available to extract verbatim quotes and arXiv IDs for loophole papers. Quantitative per-mechanism constraints remain open. Direction d-06 asked what non-standard physics would be needed to save an eV sterile neutrino (a fourth neutrino with mass ~1 eV) given the cosmological limit on extra radiation. The answer is that standard cosmology excludes it, and any loophole must suppress its contribution by more than a factor of three and is itself constrained. What was established: - The cosmological limit is N_eff (effective number of relativistic species, where the Standard Model predicts 3.044) = 2.99 +/- 0.17 from Planck 2018 TT,TE,EE+lowE+lensing+BAO. This implies Delta N_eff (extra radiation beyond the Standard Model) < 0.28 at 95% confidence (Gaussian 1.96 sigma upper limit on observed Delta = -0.054 +/- 0.17). A fully thermalized eV sterile contributes Delta N_eff = 1.0, so it must be suppressed by a factor >3.6 (1.0/0.28) to survive. - Two anchor points were computed locally with predict_sterile_nu (Dodelson-Widrow production, no lepton asymmetry): the canonical BEST short-baseline best fit (m_s = 1.14 eV, sin^2 2theta = 0.42, where sin^2 2theta measures mixing with active neutrinos) gives Delta N_eff = 1.0, total N_eff = 4.044, relic density Omega_s h^2 = 29.3 (244 times the observed dark matter 0.12), BBN helium mass fraction Yp = 0.2596 versus observed 0.2449 +/- 0.004 and deuterium D/H = 2.78e-5 versus 2.547 +/- 0.025e-5, Delta chi^2_BBN = 23.1 versus Standard Model (threshold 3.84 at 95%), excluded at 6.2 sigma versus Planck. A low-mixing threshold point (m_s = 1.0 eV, sin^2 2theta = 0.001) gives Delta N_eff = 0.40, N_eff = 3.44, Omega_s h^2 = 0.055, Delta chi^2 = 0.62 (allowed by BBN but still above the 0.28 CMB limit, 2.7 sigma tension). - Three classes of loopholes were identified from four web_search calls (2024-2026 literature snippets): large lepton asymmetry (primordial neutrino-antineutrino asymmetry L ~ 1e-2, especially flavor-asymmetric with near-zero total asymmetry that can evade BBN/CMB via oscillation equilibration), secret neutrino self-interactions (new interactions that generate finite-temperature suppression of active-sterile mixing), and low reheating temperature (reheating after inflation below the sterile production peak, so thermalization never completes). Each can in principle reduce Delta N_eff from 1.0 to <0.28 but is independently limited by BBN Yp/D/H, CMB free-streaming, structure formation, and collider constraints. - Viability statement: eV 3+1 sterile neutrinos are excluded in standard cosmology; they remain viable only with non-standard suppression that is itself constrained and requires tuned parameters. What ran and where: describe_sterile_nu_tools and two predict_sterile_nu evaluations ran locally; four web_search queries ran for literature leads. Existing artifacts were reused from /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-sbl-neff/runs/261107_171616/ including bbn_vs_neff.png (Figure 1, Yp and D/H versus N_eff) and exclusion_scan_DW_9bdb63.png (Figure 2, 3600-point exclusion plane) and scan_DW_9bdb63.csv/.npz. What was not done: No read_arxiv_chunk or cite calls executed due to tool budget exhaustion (0 calls remaining), so the required 2-3 verbatim citations with arXiv IDs/DOIs and per-loophole quantitative limits (required L values, coupling strengths, T_RH thresholds) could not be provided. Web search snippets are not citable sources.
