**Blocked — Complete literature survey 2024-2026 SBL status with 5 verbatim citations including arXiv:2504.16590 and 1-2 extracted figures.** Tool budget exhausted after web_search calls (3 DNS failures for wt.wikipedia.org.cels.anl.gov); no read_arxiv_chunk, cite, or get_paper_figures executions possible. Local paper cache miss for /tmp/arXiv_2504.16590.txt confirmed. Board findings f-023, f-026, f-027, f-028 and dead end x-04 recorded with available tc- ids. Direction d-04 asked for a 2024-2026 short-baseline sterile neutrino literature survey with 5 verbatim arXiv citations including arXiv:2504.16590 and 1-2 extracted figures. Web search established the qualitative status but tool budget prevented read_arxiv_chunk, cite, and get_paper_figures. STEREO final 119 reactor-on days (Oct 2017-Nov 2020, 107,588 antineutrinos at 2.5-7 m from ILL highly enriched uranium reactor) shows no distance over energy oscillation and excludes the canonical reactor anomaly eV sterile region at greater than 99.9 percent confidence level. MicroBooNE 170-ton liquid argon time projection chamber on the Booster beam saw no electron neutrino excess 2021-2024; June 2024 combined analysis excluded the MiniBooNE electron neutrino interpretation at greater than 99 percent confidence level and December 2025 two-beam data exclude the single light sterile LSND/MiniBooNE interpretation at 95 percent confidence level. PROSPECT (segmented detector about 7 m from High Flux Isotope Reactor) plus STEREO combined spectra are compatible with chi-squared over degrees of freedom 24.1 over 21 and exclude most reactor anomaly space; the 5 to 6 percent rate deficit and 5 MeV bump are attributed to flux prediction biases. Gallium anomaly (GALLEX/SAGE chromium-51 calibration) confirmed by BEST at greater than 5 sigma, consistent with mass splitting about 1 eV squared and mixing about 0.4, but in tension with reactor and accelerator nulls; arXiv:2504.16590 proposes an independent test using the same chromium-51 source via electron neutrino scattering. No .bib file with verbatim quotes was created and no figures with captions were saved in this direction. Existing quantitative BBN and cosmic microwave background artifacts remain in /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-sbl-neff/runs/261107_171616/ including the 3600-point scan and exclusion plane figure 2. Remaining open: 5 validated citations, verbatim quotes, and 1-2 published figures are required to meet success criteria.
