**Completed — Reuse existing 3600-point scan/grid artifacts for exclusion-plane overlay with SBL contours and robustness statistics.** Direction d-05 reused existing 3600-point scan and grid artifacts without new heavy jobs. All files verified in runs/261107_171616: scan_DW_9bdb63.csv/.npz (3600 points, m_s 0.1-10 eV, sin^2 2theta 1e-4 to 1), sterile_nu_grid_DW_1ddeb2.csv (49 points) and sterile_nu_grid_DW_b2a7f6.csv (27-point thermalization threshold grid). Standard-cosmology assumption documented: Dodelson-Widrow production with zero lepton asymmetry and no secret interactions, BBN fit valid for N_eff 2.044-6.044, omega_b h2 0.019-0.0257, m_s below about 100 keV, exclusion Delta chi2 vs Standard Model above 3.84 at 95 percent confidence. Threshold confirmed: mixing of 0.001 gives extra radiation Delta N_eff 0.40 (total N_eff 3.44, Delta chi2 0.62 allowed) while 0.003 gives Delta N_eff 1.0 (total N_eff 4.044, Delta chi2 23.1 excluded) for all eV masses 0.5, 1 and 3 eV. Fully thermalized case predicts helium mass fraction Yp 0.2596 versus observed 0.2449 plus/minus 0.004 (3.7 sigma high) and deuterium D/H 2.777e-5 versus 2.547 plus/minus 0.025e-5 (9.2 sigma high), slopes dYp/dN_eff 0.0135 and dD/H/dN_eff 0.331e-5 per unit N_eff, BBN alone limits Delta N_eff below 0.55 at 95 percent. Robustness: 2597 of 3600 points (72 percent) BBN-excluded and 2362 of 3600 (66 percent) overclose relic density above 0.12, maximum allowed mixing 0.00122 at all eV masses. Exclusion plane figure regenerated as Figure 2 exclusion_scan_DW_9bdb63.png from existing NPZ. All short-baseline preferred regions (BEST about 0.4, reactor about 0.09, LSND/MiniBooNE 0.01 to 0.5 at Delta m2 about 1 eV2) lie 8 to 400 times above allowed maximum and deep in excluded region. compute_statistics via load_table_data failed because tool only searches input directory, verified instead by direct file reads. SBL contour digitization not executed as literature figures not extracted in companion direction.
