**Blocked — Quantify non-standard loopholes required to reconcile eV sterile with N_eff=2.99+/-0.17 and their independent constraints.** Tool budget exhausted before read_arxiv_chunk/cite could run; 2-3 verbatim citations with per-loophole quantitative limits remain open. Direction d-06 asked what non-standard physics would be needed to save an eV sterile neutrino (a fourth neutrino with mass ~1 eV) given cosmological limits on extra radiation. Standard cosmology excludes it; any loophole must suppress its contribution by more than a factor of three and is itself constrained. What was established: - The cosmological limit is N_eff (effective number of relativistic species, Standard Model predicts 3.044) = 2.99 +/- 0.17 from Planck 2018 TT,TE,EE+lowE+lensing+BAO. This implies Delta N_eff (extra radiation beyond Standard Model) < 0.28 at 95% confidence (Gaussian 1.96 sigma upper limit on observed Delta = -0.054 +/- 0.17). A fully thermalized eV sterile contributes Delta N_eff = 1.0, so it must be suppressed by factor >3.6 (1.0/0.28) to survive. - Two anchor points computed locally with predict_sterile_nu (Dodelson-Widrow production, no lepton asymmetry): canonical BEST short-baseline best fit (m_s = 1.14 eV, sin^2 2theta = 0.42, where sin^2 2theta measures mixing with active neutrinos) gives Delta N_eff = 1.0, total N_eff = 4.044, relic density Omega_s h^2 = 29.3 (244 times observed dark matter 0.12), BBN helium mass fraction Yp = 0.2596 versus observed 0.2449 +/- 0.004 and deuterium D/H = 2.78e-5 versus 2.547 +/- 0.025e-5, Delta chi^2_BBN = 23.1 versus Standard Model (threshold 3.84 at 95%), excluded at 6.2 sigma versus Planck. Low-mixing threshold point (m_s = 1.0 eV, sin^2 2theta = 0.001) gives Delta N_eff = 0.40, N_eff = 3.44, Omega_s h^2 = 0.055, Delta chi^2 = 0.62 (allowed by BBN but still above 0.28 CMB limit, 2.7 sigma tension). - Three loophole classes identified from web_search literature leads (2024-2026 snippets, not citable): large lepton asymmetry L ~ 1e-2 (especially flavor-asymmetric with near-zero total asymmetry washed out by oscillations at MeV, evading BBN/CMB), secret neutrino self-interactions (finite-temperature suppression of active-sterile mixing), and low reheating temperature T_RH << 100 MeV (production never completes). Each can in principle reduce Delta N_eff from 1.0 to <0.28 but is independently limited by BBN Yp/D/H, CMB free-streaming, structure formation and laboratory bounds. - Viability statement: eV 3+1 sterile neutrinos are excluded in standard cosmology; viable only with non-standard suppression that is itself constrained and requires tuned parameters. What ran and where: describe_sterile_nu_tools and two predict_sterile_nu evaluations ran locally; four web_search queries ran for literature leads. Existing artifacts reused from /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-sbl-neff/runs/261107_171616/ including bbn_vs_neff.png (Figure 1, Yp and D/H versus N_eff) and exclusion_scan_DW_9bdb63.png (Figure 2, 3600-point exclusion plane) and scan_DW_9bdb63.csv/.npz. No new output files were written in this direction. What was not done and remains open: No read_arxiv_chunk or cite calls executed due to tool budget exhaustion, so required 2-3 verbatim citations with arXiv IDs/DOIs and per-loophole quantitative limits (required L values, coupling strengths, T_RH thresholds) could not be provided. Web search snippets are not citable sources. Recorded as dead end x-06.
