**Blocked — Complete literature survey 2024-2026 SBL status with 5 verbatim citations including arXiv:2504.16590 and 1-2 extracted figures.** Tool budget exhausted after web_search; read_arxiv_chunk, cite, and get_paper_figures could not run to produce 5 verbatim citations and 1-2 extracted figures. DNS failures also blocked some searches. Direction d-04 asked whether eV-scale sterile neutrinos remain viable given 2024-2026 short-baseline results and BBN/CMB limits. Quantitative BBN/CMB exclusion is established; literature survey with 5 verbatim citations and 1-2 extracted figures is blocked by tool budget. What was established and where it ran: - All quantitative work ran locally via the sterile-neutrino server and is saved in /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-sbl-neff/runs/261107_171616/. Files verified: scan_DW_9bdb63.csv and scan_DW_9bdb63.npz (3600-point scan, m_s 0.1-10 eV, sin^2 2theta 1e-4 to 1), sterile_nu_grid_DW_1ddeb2.csv (49-point grid), sterile_nu_grid_DW_b2a7f6.csv (27-point thermalization threshold grid), Figure 1 bbn_vs_neff.png (Yp and D/H vs N_eff) and Figure 2 exclusion_scan_DW_9bdb63.png (BBN-excluded and overclosure regions). - Canonical BEST short-baseline best fit (sterile mass m_s = 1.14 eV, mass splitting Delta m^2 = 1.3 eV^2, mixing sin^2 2theta = 0.42, where mixing measures active-sterile coupling) fully thermalizes in standard Dodelson-Widrow cosmology (no lepton asymmetry) to extra radiation Delta N_eff = 1.0, total N_eff = 4.044. This is excluded at 6.2 sigma versus Planck+ACT+DESI N_eff = 2.99 +/- 0.17 (Standard Model 3.044) and at Delta chi^2_BBN = 23.1 versus Standard Model (95% threshold 3.84), with helium mass fraction Yp = 0.2596 versus observed 0.2449 +/- 0.004 and deuterium D/H = 2.78e-5 versus 2.547 +/- 0.025e-5, and relic density Omega_s h^2 = 29.3 versus observed dark matter 0.12 (244 times too high). - Thermalization threshold: for eV masses 0.5, 1, 3 eV, mixing sin^2 2theta = 0.001 gives Delta N_eff = 0.40 (Delta chi^2 = 0.62, allowed by BBN but 2.7 sigma high versus Planck), while sin^2 2theta >= 0.003 gives Delta N_eff = 1.0 (excluded). Maximum BBN-allowed mixing is sin^2 2theta = 0.00122 at all sampled eV masses. Full scan: 2597 of 3600 points (72%) BBN-excluded and 2362 of 3600 (66%) overclose. BBN impact slopes are dYp/dN_eff = 0.0135 and dD/H/dN_eff = 0.331e-5 per unit N_eff; BBN alone limits Delta N_eff < 0.55 at 95%. - Literature status from web_search (not citable, no verbatim quotes): STEREO final 119 reactor-on-day dataset (Dec 2024, 2.5-7 m baselines from ILL highly enriched uranium reactor) shows no distance-over-energy oscillation and excludes canonical reactor anomaly eV-sterile region at >99.9% CL. MicroBooNE 170-ton liquid-argon time projection chamber on Booster beam saw no electron-neutrino excess; June 2024 combined analysis excluded MiniBooNE electron-neutrino interpretation at >99% CL and Dec 2025 two-beam data exclude single light sterile LSND/MiniBooNE at 95% CL. PROSPECT (segmented detector ~7 m from HFIR) + STEREO combined spectra are compatible with chi^2/dof 24.1/21 and exclude most reactor anomaly space, attributing 5-6% rate deficit and 5 MeV bump to flux-prediction biases. Gallium anomaly (GALLEX/SAGE/BEST >5 sigma, Delta m^2 ~1 eV^2, sin^2 2theta ~0.4) persists in tension with nulls; arXiv:2504.16590 (Ciuffoli et al., Apr 2025, Testing the Gallium anomaly using Electron-Neutrino Scattering) proposes independent test using same chromium-51 source via electron-neutrino scattering. What was not done and remains open: - No read_arxiv_chunk, cite, or get_paper_figures calls executed due to tool budget exhaustion (4 calls remaining at handoff, then 0). No .bib file with 5 verbatim quotes including arXiv:2504.16590 was created and no published figures with captions were saved, so success criteria are unmet. DNS failures on some web_search calls further limited arXiv ID resolution. Board posts f-035 to f-040 and dead end x-07 record the partial results.
