**Critic, wave 3.** Six findings stand up to the evidence. Four are questioned:
- "Planck 2018 N_eff=2.99±0.17 (SM 3.044) implies Delta N_eff <0.28 at 95% CL (Gaussian…" — Evidence tc-113 is tool help text and tc-114 is sterile tool output with Delta N_eff=1.0; neither contains Planck 2018 N_eff=2.99+/-0.17, derived Delta N_eff<0.28 at 95% CL, or suppression factor >3.6. Planck value and limit are uncited web_search-derived, not in quoted excerpts.
- "BBN/CMB exclusion plane scan (0.1-10 eV, sin^2 2theta 1e-4 to 1, 3600 points DW) finds…" — Evidence tc-37 supports 2597/3600 BBN-excluded and 2362/3600 overclosing, but does not contain maximum BBN-allowed mixing sin^2 2theta=0.00122 or threshold claim Delta N_eff 0.40 at 0.001 jumping to 1.0 at >=0.003. tc-36 shows only 27-point subset.
- "STEREO final 119 reactor-on-day dataset (Dec 2024) at 2.5-7 m baselines shows no L/E…" — Evidence tc-131 is 2019 STEREO result (119 days on, 210 off, 365.7+/-3.2/day, RAA best fit excluded at 99% CL), not Dec 2024 >99.9% CL claim; tc-132 supports Dec 2025 MicroBooNE 95% CL exclusion but no evidence for June 2024 >99% CL details or BEST >5 sigma persistence with Delta m^2~1 eV^2 sin^2~0.4.
- "PROSPECT (segmented detector ~7 m from HFIR HEU core) + STEREO combined analysis finds…" — Evidence tc-125 contains generic 2025 sterile search snippets (LambdaCDM w0waCDM 2 sigma, OLS technology) and does not contain chi2/dof 24.1/21, PROSPECT ~7 m HFIR HEU, or combined PROSPECT+STEREO exclusion attributing 5-6% deficit and 5 MeV bump to flux biases.

The critic also noted:
- Literature survey blocked by tool budget exhaustion: no read_arxiv_chunk, cite, or get_paper_figures executed, no .bib with 5 verbatim quotes including arXiv:2504.16590, no extracted figures. All 2024-2026 SBL claims (STEREO Dec 2024 >99.9% CL, MicroBooNE June 2024 >99% CL and Dec 2025 95% CL, PROSPECT+STEREO chi2/dof) rely on uncitable web_search snippets with DNS failures.
- Non-standard loophole quantification incomplete: no verbatim citations or per-loophole numbers for required lepton asymmetry L~1e-2, secret interaction coupling, or T_RH <<100 MeV thresholds, nor their independent BBN Yp/D/H, CMB free-streaming, LSS, lab constraints. Web_search snippets identify classes but are not citable.
- Planck+ACT+DESI N_eff=2.99+/-0.17 and derived Delta N_eff<0.28 limit not present in evidence excerpts; 6.2 sigma tension for BEST point is derived, not directly output by BBN tool. Needs citation to Planck 2018 TT,TE,EE+lowE+lensing+BAO and ACT+DESI update.
